# Land Rover Discovery 3 five-door, 2004-2009.
#
# The third Discovery (LR3): the all-new integrated body-frame shell, the
# smooth rounded flanks, the stepped roofline and the horizontal tail lamps.
# The five-door is modelled.
# https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/Land_Rover_Discovery
#
# Dimensions 4.849 x 1.915 x 1.882 m (2005-06) or 1.892 m (2007-09),
# wheelbase 2.885 m.
#
# Shape reference: image 1 is the side profile; the front and rear
# three-quarters show the lamps, grille and tailgate.
#
# Colours: grade (b), factory-derived names from a Land Rover parts
# catalogue, but the page is plainly incomplete (five names only). Java
# Black, Zermatt Silver, Chawton White and Bonatti Grey are used; Zermatt
# Silver rests on grade (d) evidence. Weights 12, 10, 10, 8, total 40,
# provisional.
#
# Speed 190 km/h. Comfort 85/307, on the line 180 + 1.5 x 85. Classes 3,4.
# Dates are road presence: 2004 intro, retires staggered 2025-2028.
#
# Metres master: citycars/4.5/land-rover-discovery-3.blend. Interchange:
# citycars/4.5/land-rover-discovery-3.dae. References:
# citycars/references/land-rover-discovery-3/ (gitignored; Wikimedia Commons).
#
# Accepted deviations: the rear quarter glass is a rectangular panel rather than
# the shaped window, and the arch cladding is a flat ribbon. Badges and tailgate
# lettering are below pak resolution and omitted. At 128 px the forward-leaning
# C-pillar, roof step and asymmetric tailgate read as a Discovery 3.


obj=citycar
name=LandRoverDiscovery3(JavaBlack)
copyright=JamesPetts

DistributionWeight=12
intro_year=2004
intro_month=6
retire_year=2028
retire_month=6
speed=190
class=3,4
maximum_comfortable_journey_minutes=85
maximum_tolerable_journey_minutes=307

Image[E]=./images/land-rover-discovery-3-javablack_E.0.0,-33,14
Image[SE]=./images/land-rover-discovery-3-javablack_SE.0.0,-13,0
Image[S]=./images/land-rover-discovery-3-javablack_S.0.0,0,0
